"Munis \u00f7 intake logs","exists_today":"possible"}},"mandate":{"status":"required to receive funding","citation":"Maryland Family Network Family Support Center grant"},"strategic_linkage":"Livable Frederick \u00b7 strong, supported families and school readiness","alignment":"direct","twenty_percent":{"minus":"Evening and Saturday hours end and one home-visiting caseload closes; about 70 families move to a waitlist.","plus":"A second drop-in site opens in the Golden Mile corridor, adding roughly 120 families."},"is_admin":false},{"name":"Child Advocacy Center","facing":"external","statement":"Child Advocacy Center delivers forensic interviews, victim advocacy, and coordinated medical and mental-health referral to children who have disclosed abuse and their non-offending caregivers so that children are interviewed once, protected, and connected to treatment","beneficiary":"About 450 child victims and their caregivers a year, referred by law enforcement and Child Protective Services countywide","fte":8.5,"item_ids":[2,3,4,6,8,9,11,17,24,34,39,73,78,79,88,89,90,95,99,101,103,106,107,108,110,116,117,118,124,134,149,163,164,174],"allocation_note":"Three costing centers roll up: the General Fund CAC center (staff), the CAC Services grant (training, dues, contracted therapy), and VOCA, which funds victim advocates and in-kind salary match. The multidisciplinary team's investigators and prosecutors are not costed here.","contributing_divisions":"Sheriff's Office and Frederick Police (investigators); State's Attorney (prosecution); Department of Social Services (CPS caseworkers); Frederick Health (medical exams)","measures":{"result":{"metric":"Share of children referred to treatment who begin services within 30 days","source":"NCAtrak case management","exists_today":"likely"},"volume":{"metric":"Forensic interviews conducted and advocacy contacts","source":"NCAtrak","exists_today":"likely"},"unit_cost":{"metric":"Cost per child served","source":"Munis \u00f7 NCAtrak","exi